From 596b955d68568265bd444a6ce0d54d1e276b7dfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Wang <Henry.Wang@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Jul 2022 05:29:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xen/arm: Introduce detection of MPAM Memory-System
 Component (MSC)

A Memory-System Component (MSC) is a function, unit, or design block
in a memory system that can have partitionable resources. MSCs consist
of all units that handle load or store requests issued by any MPAM
Requester. An MSC has resources that are used to process memory
requests, and therefore the use of a resource can be controlled. SMMUs,
caches, TLBs and memory channel controllers are examples of an MSC.
From a software viewpoint, an MSC is a container of resources.

This commit introduces a function `mpam_msc_probe()`, and the MPAM boot
time initialization starts from there. In this patch, we start from
probing the number of MSCs in firmware (device tree). This is based on
checking the compatible property of each device node, which should match
"arm,mpam-msc" according to the spec.

Signed-off-by: Henry Wang <Henry.Wang@arm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
Issue-Id: SCM-5049
Change-Id: Ia772777a31d0e43e815daccbb15c64e03bdfcb65
---
 xen/arch/arm/mpam.c        | 81 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 xen/arch/arm/setup.c       |  5 +++
 xen/include/asm-arm/mpam.h | 22 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 108 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xen/arch/arm/mpam.c
 create mode 100644 xen/include/asm-arm/mpam.h

diff --git a/xen/arch/arm/mpam.c b/xen/arch/arm/mpam.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..3df0f59997
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xen/arch/arm/mpam.c
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
+/*
+ * xen/arch/arm/mpam.c
+ *
+ * Code of the Arm MPAM (Memory Partitioning And Monitoring) extension support.
+ *
+ * Copyright (C) 2022 Arm Ltd.
+ *
+ * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
+ * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 2 as
+ * published by the Free Software Foundation.
+ *
